# type: (Text) -> Text
"""Normalize a path.

This function normalizes a given path by collapsing back-references (such as
"..") and removing duplicated separators ("/"). If the input describes a
path that can not be reached, such as "foo/../../bar", an IndexError will be
excepted and the function will raise an illegal back reference instead.

:param path:
    The path to be normalized. For example, "/foo//bar/frob/../baz".

:return:
    A valid file system path. For example, '/foo/bar/baz'.

"""
if path == "":
    return path
if path.startswith("//"):
    path = path[1:]
if path.endswith("/"):
    path = path[:-1]
